<urn:atm:triage:finding/AM3-STALE-DOCS-LEGACY-PATHS>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "AM3-STALE-DOCS-LEGACY-PATHS" ;
  triage:title "Several docs/atm-daemon/*.md files still present deleted local_ipc_transport.rs/local_ipc_connection.rs/composition.rs paths as current, in-scope files" ;
  triage:description "AM.3's Deliverable 1 explicitly names 'docs' as an in-scope deletion target alongside the code. docs/atm-daemon/recovery-text-rules.md's File Ownership Map, docs/atm-daemon/observability.md and docs/atm-daemon/architecture.md's migration-target sections, and docs/atm-daemon/boundaries.md all still present local_ipc_transport.rs, local_ipc_connection.rs, and/or composition.rs as live, current file paths, without any 'retired'/'historical' marker -- contrast with boundaries/atm-daemon/socket-server-transport.toml's status.state = \"retired\" or the 'Historical: PeerClientTransportAdapter' section elsewhere, which correctly mark superseded content. Found by ruthless-boundary-qa during this round's review. RECHECK (QA-AM3-2, 2026-08-10, commit 6fe17eeb): PARTIALLY FIXED. The originally-cited occurrence (boundaries.md) plus recovery-text-rules.md and observability.md and architecture.md were all correctly updated with explicit retired/historical markers -- confirmed by quality-mgr's own direct read. However, ruthless-boundary-qa, arch-qa, and req-qa all independently (3 of 4 QA-2 reviewers) identified the identical unmarked-live-reference defect surviving in two sibling files not touched by the fix commit: docs/atm-daemon/state-diagrams.md:19 ('Current implementation seam: crates/atm-daemon/src/composition.rs') and docs/atm-daemon/startup-state-machine.md:38-41,57,65-66 (lists composition.rs/RuntimeComposition::start/RuntimeLifecycle as the live daemon runtime lifecycle root/code owner). Independently confirmed by quality-mgr via direct read. Remains open with expanded occurrence scope; still minor/non-blocking." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-am" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "doc-gap" ;
